# Video Feedback — All Changes

## Overview

Two rounds of changes: initial implementation, then bug fixes for frame sync, preprocessing offsets, and browser codec.

---

## New Files

### [video_feedback.py](file:///c:/Users/marto/Documents/egyetem/szakdoga/szakdolgozat/model/comparison/video_feedback.py)

Core renderer that generates a side-by-side MP4. Key design:
- Reads **all frames sequentially** with the same FPS resampling logic as [extractor.py](file:///c:/Users/marto/Documents/egyetem/szakdoga/szakdolgozat/model/extraction/extractor.py) — avoids unreliable `cv2.CAP_PROP_POS_FRAMES` seeking
- Uses `preprocess_info` offsets to map DTW alignment indices back to original HDF5 frame indices
- Draws green skeleton on both dancers + blue ghost of teacher on student's side
- Writes with `mp4v`, then **re-encodes to H.264** via `imageio-ffmpeg` for browser compatibility
- Caps output height at **720px**

### [VideoFeedback.tsx](file:///c:/Users/marto/Documents/egyetem/szakdoga/szakdolgozat/view/src/components/VideoFeedback.tsx)

MUI-styled video player component. Renders an HTML5 `<video>` element with native controls. Fetches from `http://localhost:8001/feedback/video?session_id=...`.

### [test_video_feedback.py](file:///c:/Users/marto/Documents/egyetem/szakdoga/szakdolgozat/model/comparison/test_video_feedback.py)

Synthetic test suite (creates fake videos + HDF5 data, verifies output MP4 dimensions/frame count).

